  "scope": "Both existing native human appearances: strand/cutout/brow response, brown iris mask/color, skin specular response and reuse of independent appearance materials. Geometry, rig, clothing, nine morphs, ten clips and save schema remain unchanged.",
  "implemented": [
    "Authored hair atlas receives local strand separation and restrained tangent relief, mip-aware fade, alpha-to-coverage plus cutout fallback. Eyebrows use their own matte response. No source bitmap is repainted.",
    "The old approximate brown-atlas correction centers left red crescents. Pupil centroids and saturated iris radii were measured from the unchanged CC0 image. Both 32 perimeter sectors and untouched sclera are checked in native rendered pixels.",
    "Skin keeps the original color atlas and roughness; restrained dielectric specular replaces the stronger default. Experimental four-map Blender skin bake is not integrated.",
    "Material keys depend only on the category used by that material. Unrelated cloth/eye/height/build selections reuse hair and skin objects. Both families retain 60 cached materials after the tested choices, with no growth on repetition."
  ],
